WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.130 --> 00:00:02.180
- I feel like everybody at some point

00:00:02.180 --> 00:00:06.560
in their life has met somebody
who was truly inspiring.

00:00:06.560 --> 00:00:08.690
They seem to have their life figured out.

00:00:08.690 --> 00:00:09.900
They are determined.

00:00:09.900 --> 00:00:12.220
They can carve out their own destiny.

00:00:12.220 --> 00:00:13.910
They create their own luck.

00:00:13.910 --> 00:00:16.990
And on the flip side, a lot
of us have met people who seem

00:00:16.990 --> 00:00:18.910
to just bury themselves in a hole

00:00:18.910 --> 00:00:20.990
and are unable to get out of it.

00:00:20.990 --> 00:00:23.320
They are unable to
recognize the opportunities

00:00:23.320 --> 00:00:24.330
in front of them,

00:00:24.330 --> 00:00:26.920
they harbor a lot of
negativity towards life

00:00:26.920 --> 00:00:29.590
and they seem perpetually stuck.

00:00:29.590 --> 00:00:33.660
Helpless against seemingly
endless negative external forces.

00:00:33.660 --> 00:00:36.810
And I feel like a lot of people
talk about these two types

00:00:36.810 --> 00:00:40.460
of people and try to
distill one single belief

00:00:40.460 --> 00:00:43.680
or concept that separates the two of them.

00:00:43.680 --> 00:00:45.440
And if you just adopt this belief

00:00:45.440 --> 00:00:47.810
then you'll be like the successful person

00:00:47.810 --> 00:00:49.900
and not like the unsuccessful person.

00:00:49.900 --> 00:00:52.230
But I feel like it's a
little foolish to do so

00:00:52.230 --> 00:00:55.790
because everybody's life is
so well wildly different.

00:00:55.790 --> 00:00:57.290
People had different upbringings.

00:00:57.290 --> 00:01:00.680
People have such different
instilled beliefs

00:01:00.680 --> 00:01:03.440
about the world or religion or whatever.

00:01:03.440 --> 00:01:06.500
It's hard to just say
that one single belief

00:01:06.500 --> 00:01:09.650
will change someone's life
for the better for eternity

00:01:09.650 --> 00:01:12.090
and they'll never
experience hardship again.

00:01:12.090 --> 00:01:16.260
But I have noticed one trait
that successful people seem

00:01:16.260 --> 00:01:19.840
to share more often than
unsuccessful people.

00:01:19.840 --> 00:01:21.890
And I can't help but think that there

00:01:21.890 --> 00:01:25.530
is a strong correlation
between having that belief

00:01:25.530 --> 00:01:27.750
and having success in life.

00:01:27.750 --> 00:01:30.830
And that is that successful
people tend to have

00:01:30.830 --> 00:01:33.430
an internal locus of control.

00:01:33.430 --> 00:01:37.170
And less successful people
tend to have an external one.

00:01:37.170 --> 00:01:38.890
So what is locus of control?

00:01:38.890 --> 00:01:41.100
Locus of control is the degree

00:01:41.100 --> 00:01:43.620
to which people believe that they,

00:01:43.620 --> 00:01:45.920
as opposed to external forces,

00:01:45.920 --> 00:01:49.480
have control over the outcome
of events in their lives.

00:01:49.480 --> 00:01:52.010
So, you watching this
right now either have

00:01:52.010 --> 00:01:53.860
an external locus of control

00:01:53.860 --> 00:01:55.200
or an internal locus of control.

00:01:55.200 --> 00:01:58.760
And I think the severity
of either of these extremes

00:01:58.760 --> 00:02:02.250
was formed through your
childhood and your development

00:02:02.250 --> 00:02:04.470
and your transition into adulthood.

00:02:04.470 --> 00:02:07.750
Because children, very
young children especially,

00:02:07.750 --> 00:02:09.970
have an extra internal locus of control.

00:02:09.970 --> 00:02:13.140
External forces have
control over the outcomes

00:02:13.140 --> 00:02:14.630
of events in their lives.

00:02:14.630 --> 00:02:15.463
When you're a kid,

00:02:15.463 --> 00:02:17.860
you're pretty much absolutely helpless,

00:02:17.860 --> 00:02:20.310
especially when you're a very young kid.

00:02:20.310 --> 00:02:23.250
You can't really feed
yourself, or clothe yourself.

00:02:23.250 --> 00:02:26.720
You're so dependent on a
parental figure to provide you

00:02:26.720 --> 00:02:29.830
with all of your needs that
you basically have no choice

00:02:29.830 --> 00:02:33.000
but to develop a very
external locus of control.

00:02:33.000 --> 00:02:36.660
The situations of your life are
entirely out of your control

00:02:36.660 --> 00:02:40.170
and you're entirely dependent
on some sort of third party

00:02:40.170 --> 00:02:42.840
to provide you with what
you need to survive.

00:02:42.840 --> 00:02:44.060
And there's nothing wrong with that,

00:02:44.060 --> 00:02:46.250
like, kids don't really have a choice

00:02:46.250 --> 00:02:47.830
in the matter, that is their world.

00:02:47.830 --> 00:02:51.420
That's a factual and realistic
belief to have as a kid.

00:02:51.420 --> 00:02:54.770
But hopefully you had a
competent parental figure

00:02:54.770 --> 00:02:56.930
or a leader as you're growing up

00:02:56.930 --> 00:03:00.270
that kind of taught you the
ropes, how to, how to clean,

00:03:00.270 --> 00:03:03.600
how to make money, how to fend
for yourself in the world.

00:03:03.600 --> 00:03:06.400
I've always thought that if a
parent does their job right,

00:03:06.400 --> 00:03:08.550
they basically phase themselves out.

00:03:08.550 --> 00:03:10.330
Hopefully by the time you're an adult,

00:03:10.330 --> 00:03:11.860
you still want your parents around,

00:03:11.860 --> 00:03:13.460
but you don't need them around.

00:03:13.460 --> 00:03:15.750
If they were to die, you'd be okay.

00:03:15.750 --> 00:03:17.180
Like you could fend for yourself.

00:03:17.180 --> 00:03:18.530
You can figure stuff out.

00:03:18.530 --> 00:03:20.260
But unfortunately for a lot of us,

00:03:20.260 --> 00:03:22.440
we bring a lot of the helplessness

00:03:22.440 --> 00:03:24.800
of childhood into adulthood.

00:03:24.800 --> 00:03:27.460
We never shake the idea that we need

00:03:27.460 --> 00:03:29.210
to be provided for somehow.

00:03:29.210 --> 00:03:32.940
We remain dependent on some
sort of external system

00:03:32.940 --> 00:03:35.770
to provide us with the necessary materials

00:03:35.770 --> 00:03:37.280
to survive and thrive.

00:03:37.280 --> 00:03:39.410
And a lot of the time this
is really hard to spot.

00:03:39.410 --> 00:03:41.080
From an occupational standpoint,

00:03:41.080 --> 00:03:45.490
sometimes this can look like
being unsatisfied with your job

00:03:45.490 --> 00:03:48.700
and you're working so hard
but getting paid so little.

00:03:48.700 --> 00:03:52.500
So you externalize the
struggle onto your boss

00:03:52.500 --> 00:03:57.500
or your provider and you blame
him for your life's problems.

00:03:57.590 --> 00:04:00.880
My life sucks because my boss
doesn't see how much I'm worth

00:04:00.880 --> 00:04:02.440
and he's not paying me enough money.

00:04:02.440 --> 00:04:04.940
Or you might look at
the government and say,

00:04:04.940 --> 00:04:08.250
the government is not giving
me the proper tax breaks

00:04:08.250 --> 00:04:11.270
that I need in my societal class

00:04:11.270 --> 00:04:13.070
and it's making it really hard for me.

00:04:13.070 --> 00:04:15.480
And the tricky thing is
that a lot of the time,

00:04:15.480 --> 00:04:17.230
these are valid complaints.

00:04:17.230 --> 00:04:19.670
There's a certain amount of logic to them.

00:04:19.670 --> 00:04:23.500
But the default shouldn't
be to place all of the blame

00:04:23.500 --> 00:04:27.020
and place all of the responsibility
for changing the outcome

00:04:27.020 --> 00:04:30.310
of your life onto these external forces,

00:04:30.310 --> 00:04:32.390
otherwise we will just be imprisoned

00:04:32.390 --> 00:04:34.020
by them for our entire lives.

00:04:34.020 --> 00:04:37.880
Our default should be to look
at the cards that we are given

00:04:37.880 --> 00:04:41.630
and take full responsibility
for how we play those cards.

00:04:41.630 --> 00:04:44.480
I feel like having this
internal locus of control

00:04:44.480 --> 00:04:47.070
it's extremely important
in today's day and age

00:04:47.070 --> 00:04:48.840
because obviously in 2020

00:04:48.840 --> 00:04:50.970
we were just hit with a global pandemic

00:04:50.970 --> 00:04:55.320
and so much of that felt
so far out of our control

00:04:55.320 --> 00:04:57.140
that it was very tempting.

00:04:57.140 --> 00:05:00.560
I know for me personally
it was to develop a feeling

00:05:00.560 --> 00:05:02.700
of helplessness almost,

00:05:02.700 --> 00:05:06.030
that childlike helplessness
started to blossom again.

00:05:06.030 --> 00:05:09.550
And I felt like I had to
put my entire life on hold,

00:05:09.550 --> 00:05:11.370
put all my habits on hold

00:05:11.370 --> 00:05:13.350
until this whole pandemic blew over.

00:05:13.350 --> 00:05:15.760
Sometime halfway through I realized

00:05:15.760 --> 00:05:18.180
that I can work within this system.

00:05:18.180 --> 00:05:20.660
There are things that I can do to improve

00:05:20.660 --> 00:05:23.850
my life despite the crappy situation.

00:05:23.850 --> 00:05:26.750
And it is my sole
responsibility to figure out how

00:05:26.750 --> 00:05:30.230
to thrive within the environment
that I've been placed.

00:05:30.230 --> 00:05:33.150
It's nobody's responsibility
to come be your night

00:05:33.150 --> 00:05:36.780
and shining armor and fight
the dragons in your life.

00:05:36.780 --> 00:05:38.520
It's only your responsibility.

00:05:38.520 --> 00:05:41.360
And I don't want this to come
across like I'm scolding you,

00:05:41.360 --> 00:05:43.730
like, the father you never had.

00:05:43.730 --> 00:05:44.563
No, I'm just kidding.

00:05:44.563 --> 00:05:46.230
But hopefully to empower you.

00:05:46.230 --> 00:05:48.000
Once you start adopting more of

00:05:48.000 --> 00:05:50.000
an internal locus of control,

00:05:50.000 --> 00:05:53.940
it'll start to feel a lot less
like life is happening to you

00:05:53.940 --> 00:05:56.070
but it will start to
feel a lot more like life

00:05:56.070 --> 00:05:57.530
is happening due to you.

00:05:57.530 --> 00:05:59.830
And that's a very
empowering belief to have.

00:05:59.830 --> 00:06:01.590
In fact, I would say it's a prerequisite

00:06:01.590 --> 00:06:04.570
to making any sort of
substantial change in your life.

00:06:04.570 --> 00:06:07.190
Your positive actions
to work your way out of

00:06:07.190 --> 00:06:09.770
a bad situation, do have an impact.

00:06:09.770 --> 00:06:11.890
Your efforts are not in vain.

00:06:11.890 --> 00:06:15.270
Because not only do you have
the power to change your life,

00:06:15.270 --> 00:06:17.063
you're the only one who does.

